$DATUM 13292-87-0
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Preparation of Tri-n-octylborane. Petroleum spirits (20 mL) was added to
a flame-dried Schlenk flask and cooled to −10 °C in an ice/salt bath. A
solution of BH3·SMe2 (10 M, 2.5 mL, 25 mmol) was added with stirring,
followed by the dropwise addition of 1-octene (15.0 mL, 95.6 mmol) over 1
h. The temperature was maintained between −10 and 0 °C during this time.
The reaction mixture was allowed to come to room temperature and stirred
overnight. The volatiles were removed under vacuum for ca. 6 h to afford
BOct3. Colorless liquid, yield quantitative. 1H NMR (C6D6): δ 1.48 (m, br
overlapping, 6H, BCH2), 1.35−1.27 (m, br overlapping, 36H, CH2), 0.91 (m,
br, 9H, CH3). 13C NMR (C6D6): δ 33.64, 32.47, 30.18, 29.91 (CH2), δ 28.81
(BCH2), 25.12, 23.21 (CH2), 14.44 (CH3).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM petroleum spirits used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Thermal Dehydroboration: Experimental and Theoretical Studies of Olefin
Elimination from Trialkylboranes and Its Relationship to Alkylborane
Isomerization and Transalkylation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Weliange, Nandita M.; McGuinness, David S.; Patel, Jim
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Organometallics (2014), 33(16), 4251-4259

