$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 3. General Protocol for Hydroboration and
Diboration Experiments. All chemicals (Aldrich) were used as received. In
a typical catalytic hydroboration experiment, a solution of either HBcat
or HBpin (1.1 eq) in THF-d8 (0.5 mL) was added to a stirred mixture of
the appropriate vinylarene (30 mg) and Rh or Ir catalyst (2 mol%) in
THF-d8 (0.5 mL). The progress of the room temperature reaction was
monitored by use of 1H NMR spectroscopy, and product distributions
(quoted to the nearest 5 %, based on duplicate experiments) were
determined upon complete disappearance of the starting alkene substrate.
The identification of the hydroboration products was made possible by
comparison to authentic samples that were characterized previously by use
of multinuclear magnetic resonance techniques. Diboration reactions were
conducted in a similar fashion using B2cat2 or B2pin2. Alternatively,
reactions in which minimal consumption of the alkene was detected by use
of 1H NMR spectroscopy after 72 h at room temperature were carried out in
refluxing toluene for 72 h, whereupon the solvent was removed in vacuo
and the residual mixture was analyzed by use of 1H NMR spectroscopic
methods.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Catalytic Alkene Hydroboration Mediated by Cationic and Formally
Zwitterionic Rhodium(I) and Iridium(I) Derivatives of a P,N-Substituted
Indene
