$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Typical procedure for hydroboration of 1 a-h: Pinacolborane (2 eq) was
added to the phosphonoalkene neat at room temperature and reaction
mixture was stirred at 70°C for 1h (method A) or at 110°C for 5h (method
B) . The excess of pinacolborane was distilled under reduced pressure and
residue was chromatographed on silica gel (80:20 chloroform:ethyl
acetate). product. 1HNMR (CDCl3): δ=1.12 (m, 2H), 1.24 (s , 12H), 1.2-1.3
(m , 2H), 1.28-1.31 (t, 6H), 4.02-4.07 (q, 4H). 13CNMR (CDCl3):
δ=9.50(br),16.27, 24.31, 24.46, 61.33, 82.81. 31P (CDCl3): δ= 33.67.
11BNMR (CDCl3): δ=33.75.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Hydroboration of Unsaturated Phosphonic Esters: Synthesis of
Boronophosphonates and Trisubstituted Vinylphosphonates
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Pergament, Inna; Srebnik, Morris
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
