$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Cu-Catalyzed β-Borylation of Thioacetylenes. To a
mixture of CuCl (5.0 mg, 0.05 mmol), DPEphos (27.0 mg, 0.05 mmol),
NaOt-Bu (7.2 mg, 0.075 mmol), and B2pin2 (2a) (69.9 mg, 0.55 mmol) was
added a solution of 1a (81 mg, 0.5 mmol) in 2 mL of MeOH under a nitrogen
atmosphere. After stirring at 35 °C for 12 h, the reaction mixture was
concentrated and purified by column chromatography (petroleum ether/EtOAc
= 20:1) on silica gel to give 3a. White solid, yield 128 mg (88%). mp:
76-78 °C; Rf = 0.37 (petroleum ether/EtOAc = 20:1); 1H NMR (CDCl3, 600
MHz): δ 1.27 (s, 12H), 1.31 (t, J = 7.4 Hz, 3H), 2.79 (q, J = 7.4 Hz,
2H), 7.20-7.24 (m, 1H), 7.27 (s, 1H), 7.32-7.40 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (CDCl3,
150 MHz): δ 15.4, 24.7, 28.8, 83.5, 126.4, 127.8, 128.7, 139.6, 145.0; MS
(EI, m/z): 290 (M+, 17), 289 (4), 229 (2), 163 (8), 102 (100); HRMS (EI)
calcd for C16H23BO2S (M+) 290.1512, found 290.1511. Crystal data:
(C16H23BO2S, 290.21): monoclinic, space group P2(1)/c, a = 17.3504(16) Å
, b = 6.1246(7) Å , c = 17.8836(17) Å , U = 1691.6(3) Å 3, Z = 4, T =
296(2).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM regioselective, stereoselective, optimization study(optimized on
ligaands, copper source and solvents)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Synthesis of (Z)-1-Thio- and (Z)-2-Thio-1-alkenyl Boronates via
Copper-Catalyzed Regiodivergent Hydroboration of Thioacetylenes: An
Experimental and Theoretical Study
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Zhu, Gangguo; Kong, Wei; Feng, Hui; Qian, Zhaosheng
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2014), 79(4), 1786-1795

