$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: In a typical experiment, HBcat (40 mg, 0.34
mmol) in 0.5 mL of C6D6 was added to a solution of phenyl vinyl sulfide
(41 mg, 0.30 mmol) in 0.5 mL of C6D6 and heated at 80 °C for 8 h to
afford 9. For the catalyzed reaction the above mixture was stirred with 2
mol % RhCl(PPh3)3 at 20 °C for 8 h to give 10 in 95% NMR yield. 10,yield
95%. NMR: 1H δ 7.25-6.6 (ov m, 9H, Ph and cat), 3.02 (q, J = 8 Hz, 1H,
CH), 1.48 (d, J = 8 Hz, 3H, CH3); 11B{1H} δ 33.4 (br); 13C{1H} δ 148.4 (C
cat), 131.7, 129.1, 127.0, 123.0 (CH cat), 112.7 (CH cat), 24.0 (br,
C-B), 16.7 (CH3).
