$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Typical procedure for hydroboration of 1 a-h:
Pinacolborane (2 eq) was added to the phosphonoalkene neat at room
temperature and reaction mixture was stirred at 70°C for 1h (method A) or
at 110°C for 5h (method B) . The excess of pinacolborane was distilled
under reduced pressure and residue was chromatographed on silica gel
(80:20 chloroform:ethyl acetate). 2e 1HNMR (CDCl3): δ =0.75-0.83 (t, 2H),
1.22 (s, 12H), 1.81 (m, 2H), 2.04 (m, 2H), 1.34 (t, 6H), 3.84 (td, 1H),
4.17-4.26 (q, 4H).13C (CDCl3): δ= 10.22, 16.35, 21.20, 24.99, 34.26, 52.3
(d, J=210 Hz), 63.49, 83.28.31P (CDCl3): δ=20.64. 11BNMR (CDCl3): δ=33.62
