$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: [C5H5B(CH2)5CH3]2YCl (2). A toluene solution
of 1-hexene (453 mg, 5.38 mmol in 2 mL of toluene) was added to 1 (150
mg, 0.539 mmol) in 4 mL of toluene. After stirring for 4 days at 75 °C,
the reaction mixture was filtered. Evaporation of the orange filtrate in
vacuo left an orange oil, which was extracted with 3×2mL of hexane.
Removal of the solvent of the extract. [C5H5B(CH2)5CH3]2LuCl (10).
Following the procedure described for 2. Reaction of 9 (80 mg, 0.220
mmol) and 1-hexene (370 mg, 4.40 mmol) in 4mL of toluene for 8 days at 75
°C. 7 as an orange oil (110 mg, 94% yield). 1H NMR (400 MHz, C6D6, 25
°C): δ 7.46 (dd, J H-H = 10.0 Hz, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 4H, 3-/5-H), 7.01 (d, J
H-H = 9.6 Hz, 4H, 2-/6-H), 6.19 (t, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 2H, 4-H), 1.85-1.79
(m, 4H, B(CH 2)5CH3), 1.66-1.58 (m, 8H, B(CH 2)5CH3), 1.54-1.40 (m, 8H,
B(CH 2)5CH3), 0.98 (t, J H-H = 7.2 Hz, 6H, B(CH2)5CH 3). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
C6D6, 25 °C): δ 142.2, 132.1, 110.5, 33.3, 32.5, 28.0, 23.3, 22.6, 14.5.
11B NMR (128 MHz, C6D6, 25 °C): δ 45.3. Anal. Calcd (%) for C22H36B2ClLu:
C, 49.62; H, 6.81. Found: C, 48.99; H, 7.04.
